      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## Research recent company news before every meeting-4th August'26\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs every morning at 7 AM, prepares configuration values, and retrieves the user's meetings for the day from Google Calendar. It filters the meetings to find relevant company-related events, extracts a company name, searches NewsAPI for recent news, formats the results, and emails the briefing. If there are no qualifying meetings, the workflow ends on a no-operation fallback branch.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the schedule trigger timezone and confirm it should run daily at 7 AM.\n- Connect Google Calendar credentials and select the calendar used for meeting lookup.\n- Set any required setup fields, such as date range, attendee parsing rules, or default email recipient.\n- Add a valid NewsAPI key to the HTTP request URL or credentials and verify the query parameters match the desired freshness and sources.\n- Connect Gmail credentials and configure the sender, recipient, subject, and email body fields.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the meeting filter criteria, company-name extraction logic, NewsAPI search query, and email formatting code to match the meeting naming conventions and briefing style you prefer."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
